  {
   "title": "⚠ Common traps",
   "class": "traps",
   "col": "R",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "traps",
     "items": [
      "**Forgetting zero.** $|x|=x$ means $x\\ge 0$, so $x=0$ works too.",
      "**Losing the second case.** $|x+2|=10$ has two answers, $8$ and $-12$.",
      "**Keeping a fake answer.** A letter on the right: $x=-6$ looked fine, but fails the check.",
      "$\\sqrt{x^2}$ is $|x|$, not $x$.",
      "$|a+b|=|a|+|b|$ only when the signs are the same.",
      "$|x+6|$ is measured from $-6$, not from $6$.",
      "$-x$ is not always negative. For $x<0$ it is positive."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
